From: Haiyue Wang <haiyuewa@163.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Mar 2026 22:32:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mctp: i2c: fix skb memory leak in receive path
Git-commit: e3f5e0f22cfc2371e7471c9fd5b4da78f9df7c69
Patch-mainline: v7.0-rc4
References: CVE-2026-43457 bsc#1265000

When 'midev->allow_rx' is false, the newly allocated skb isn't consumed
by netif_rx(), it needs to free the skb directly.

Fixes: f5b8abf9fc3d ("mctp i2c: MCTP I2C binding driver")
Signed-off-by: Haiyue Wang <haiyuewa@163.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260305143240.97592-1-haiyuewa@163.com
Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni <pabeni@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: David Sterba <dsterba@suse.com>
---
 drivers/net/mctp/mctp-i2c.c |    1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/net/mctp/mctp-i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/net/mctp/mctp-i2c.c
@@ -335,6 +335,7 @@ static int mctp_i2c_recv(struct mctp_i2c
 	} else {
 		status = NET_RX_DROP;
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&midev->lock, flags);
+		kfree_skb(skb);
 	}
 
 	if (status == NET_RX_SUCCESS) {
